# Task 16 investigation fixture — profile refinement capability probe.
#
# NOTE ON NAMESPACES: the task-16 brief's illustrative snippet used
# `nitf: <https://hexplain.io/formats/nitf#>` and imported
# `<https://hexplain.io/formats/nitf>`. The actual profile at
# specification/profiles/nitf/nitf.ttl declares ontology IRI
# <https://hexplain.io/ns/profile/nitf> with preferred prefix
# `nitf: <https://hexplain.io/ns/profile/nitf#>`. This fixture uses the real
# namespace so the probe targets the actual field resource nitf:FH_FHDR.
@prefix bddo: <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#> .
@prefix nitf: <https://hexplain.io/ns/profile/nitf#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<https://example.org/nsif-probe> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "NSIF refinement probe" ;
    owl:imports <https://hexplain.io/ns/profile/nitf> .

# Probe: can a downstream profile restate a field's fixed value without redefining the
# whole struct? If the compiler takes the last-written value, refinement works. If it
# takes both, or the first, refinement needs explicit support.
nitf:FH_FHDR bddo:hasFixedValue "NSIF" .
